    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōrĭcum</span></b> , i,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a country lying between the Danube and the Alps</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 1,
			70</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōrĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Noricum, Norican</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">provincia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 63</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					34, 14, 41, § 145</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 712</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					Epod. 17, 71</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nōrĭci</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Noricans</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 24, 27, §
		146</span></i>.</div>
